<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Construction Safety & Health Management</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Protect your workforce and ensure regulatory compliance with integrated safety management that 
            embeds health and safety into the daily project workflow.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Risk Management and HIRA Logs</h2>
        <p>
            Proactively manage site hazards with integrated Hazard Identification and Risk Assessment (HIRA) 
            logs. Link digitized risk assessments directly to site work sections and schedule activities, 
            ensuring that site teams are automatically notified of specific hazards before work 
            commences on a task. Standardized risk matrices and templates ensure consistent safety 
            protocols across your entire project portfolio.
        </p>
        <p>
            Site safety plans, including emergency procedures and hospital locations, are 
            accessible to all team members via mobile, providing a centralized repository 
            for the critical safety documentation required by NSSA, OSHA, and project 
            auditors.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Safety Induction and PPE Control</h2>
        <p>
            The safety module ensures that site access is restricted to properly trained and equipped 
            personnel. Digital induction logs track safety orientation for every individual on site, 
            including specific modules for high-risk work. Integrated PPE issuance registers 
            track the assignment and replacement of safety equipment, providing an audit-ready 
            record of compliance for every site operative.
        </p>
        <p>
            Site safety inspections and "toolbox talks" are captured directly on the ground, with 
            corrective actions for safety violations assigned to responsible supervisors and 
            tracked through close-out. This transparent oversight identifies safety 
            trends and training gaps before they lead to site incidents.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Incident Reporting and Investigation</h2>
        <p>
            In the event of an incident or near-miss, the digital reporting workflow ensures that 
            critical information is captured immediately and accurately. Automatic notifications 
            alert senior management and safety officers, initiating formal investigation modules 
            guided by root-cause analysis principles. Corrective and Preventive Action (CAPA) 
            tracking ensures that lessons learned are implemented and verified.
        </p>
        <p>
            Automated generation of regulatory forms, including NSSA LD3 reports, reduces the 
            administrative burden on the safety team while ensuring that legal compliance 
            deadlines are met with precise, data-driven documentation.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

